11. Terminology Freeze

The following terms are now frozen for MOS Core v0.1.0.

Cognitive Element

The fundamental unit of cognition.

Cognitive State Space

The complete set of Cognitive Elements.

Domain

A semantic projection over cognition.

Meta-Cognitive Element

An element describing or governing cognition.

Capability

A semantic ability.

Strategy

A method for realizing a capability.

Orchestrator

A selector and coordinator of strategies.

Operation

An atomic cognitive transformation.

Transaction

A committed state transition.

Intent

A purpose driving cognition.

Decision

A chosen future action under uncertainty.

12. Missing Primitive Review

After reviewing RFC-0001 through RFC-0006, I identify only a few missing concepts.

These should NOT be added to Core yet.

They belong in later specifications.

Missing Primitive 1 — Resource Model

Needed for:

compute
storage
cost
energy
latency

Decision making eventually needs resource awareness.

Future:

RFC-0007 Resource and Economy Model
Missing Primitive 2 — Communication Model

Needed for:

multi-agent systems
distributed cognition
A2A interaction

Future:

RFC-0008 Cognitive Communication Model
Missing Primitive 3 — Identity and Trust Model

Needed for:

agents
humans
organizations
permissions

Future:

RFC-0009 Cognitive Identity Model
Missing Primitive 4 — Temporal Model

Time exists everywhere, but we have not formalized:

causality
sequence
temporal reasoning
historical reconstruction

Future:

RFC-0010 Temporal Cognition Model
Missing Primitive 5 — Evaluation and Improvement Model

Reflection exists, but formal:

benchmarks
rewards
quality measurement
self-improvement

should be separate.

Future:

RFC-0011 Cognitive Evaluation Model
